    LLM: 'Game: Dom Pedro. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Dom Pedro (Pedro) is a trick-taking card game derived from Pitch. 4-7 players (often partnerships). 52-card deck, 9 dealt. Bid for trump suit. Key scoring cards: Right Pedro (5 of trumps)=5pts, Left Pedro (same-color 5)=5pts, High(A)=1, Low(2)=1, Jack=1, Game(10)=1. Total 14pts per hand. Left Pedro counts as trump. Play to 100.',
    objective: 'Be the first team or player to reach the agreed target (commonly 100 or 62 points) by winning tricks that contain scoring trumps and by making your bid; failing the bid sets you back.',
